<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest>

    <!--
      Deliberately empty.

      Every storage grant is the host's to declare: it is the one that must ask the user, and which
      permission that is depends on the sdk it targets and on which of these filesystems it actually
      exposes. WRITE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE (maxSdkVersion 28, for LegacyMediaFileSystem) used to live
      here and now sits in :app alongside the read half.

      RequirementRules.kt names the whole set; RequirementsCheckerImpl reports an undeclared one as
      a blocker, so a host that skips a permission gets that source reported as unavailable rather
      than a grant dialog that never appears.
    -->

</manifest>
